 "summary": "The prior round's duplicate bracket-level layer (`lie_\u03b9`, `lie_mul`, `lie_mem_homogeneousSubmodule`) is gone; `AdjointAction.lean` now keeps only the definition, the `rfl` unfolding/bridge lemmas, and one specialisation each of `derivationOfEnd_\u03b9`, `map_apply_derivationOfEnd` and `derivationOfEnd_mem_homogeneousSubmodule`. Mathlib has no derivation-from-endomorphism or Lie-module structure on `SymmetricAlgebra` (only `Basic`, `Basis`, `Bialgebra/SymmetricAlgebra`), TauCeti's nearest constructions (`UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.envelopingDerivation`, `AdditiveGroup.tangentOfLinear`) target different algebras, and the new code reuses `mkDerivation`/`derivation_ext`, `LinearMap.llcomp`, `LieAlgebra.ad`, `LieRingModule.compLieHom`, `Submodule.pow_induction_on_left'` and `SetLike.mul_mem_graded`, with `Grading.lean` now consuming the new `\u03b9_mem_homogeneousSubmodule` instead of its two inline `simpa [pow_one]` clones.",
